SM-T715 tablet: no Speaker toggle on the call card.

The tablet has no earpiece, so the toggle switched nothing and read "off"
with the sound on the speaker: it is hidden. Carried forward now that this
build ships omamobile.call again (0004) and the call watchers run
(tablet-shell.json's callWatch). The armv7h series'
0007-tablet-tiles-that-work, its call-card hunk only -- the patch's scripts'
part (airplane mode through NetworkManager, the Hotspot password
notification) is already 0006 here, and its README lines named the Pixel's
modem stack. Against omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after
0001-0012; the Toggle sits five lines lower after upstream's ringing-visible
comment, and the hunk ports unchanged.

diff --git a/plugins/omamobile.call/CallCard.qml b/plugins/omamobile.call/CallCard.qml
--- a/plugins/omamobile.call/CallCard.qml
+++ b/plugins/omamobile.call/CallCard.qml
@@ -320,6 +320,8 @@
       }
       Toggle {
         objectName: "speakerToggle"
+        // SM-T715: no earpiece, so there is nothing to switch.
+        visible: false
         glyph: 0xF057E
         label: "Speaker"
         on: card.route === "speaker"
